## Capability pipelines

### pipeline_prepare

Validate a graph and return a signed quote and payment offers. No work or payment. Free steps require no wallet; paid steps require buyer wallet address. Use gas_mode=required to demand gas sponsorship or auto to prefer it. Inspect ready/blockers and gas_sponsorship. Sign offers LOCALLY, never provide a private key. Then call pipeline_invoke.

### pipeline_invoke

Execute or continue the SAME prepared graph. Submit authorizations when the signed quote enables gas_sponsorship, otherwise buyer-signed transactions; none for free steps. Never submit both payment modes. Retain run_id/access_token and the exact bundle. Pending is not failure; repeat the same run or read pipeline_status. Never create a replacement purchase after a lost response.

### pipeline_status

Read an existing pipeline, including cached signed result, without broadcasting payments or invoking providers. No wallet signer or blockchain RPC required. Inspect recovery.action for unresolved work.

HTTP: POST /studio/prepare-pipeline, then POST /ai-market/v2/invoke (hephaestus / pipeline.run@v1). Read-only recovery: GET /studio/paid-runs/{run_id}/pipeline with X-Studio-Run-Token. Preserve source_hub and the signed bundle. Maximum 16 steps. The paid Python client pays native USDC on Base 8453 or Ethereum 1; with gas_mode=required on Base the Hub sponsors gas and the buyer needs no ETH, otherwise the buyer pays gas. Free graphs need neither wallet nor RPC. Independent peer billing is rejected by preflight unless a supported settlement route exists; never substitute credits. Use ready/blockers.code to determine executability before payment. Install the released client and use aimarket-pipeline or await run_pipeline(...). See pipeline_execution in the live manifest for supported routes and the current client distribution.

Installation and full guides: https://modelmarket.dev/clients/pipeline-guide/en (also /ru, /es, /fr, /zh). Distribution metadata: https://modelmarket.dev/clients/pipeline.json.

SELLER-OP/1: active trusted peers with pinned signing keys can bill independently, without a resale account. Seller routes: POST /ai-market/v2/operations/prepare; POST /ai-market/v2/operations/{operation_id}/invoke; GET /ai-market/v2/operations/{operation_id}, with X-Operation-Token. Immutable input/wallet/payment, signed offers and durable results. Read the same operation after response loss. Uncertain downstream execution requires reconciliation; do not buy it again. See the pipeline guides (five languages) for the migrations and recovery boundaries.

Gas sponsorship (SDK 3.11.0): use gas_mode=required for direct Base USDC without buyer ETH. Sign EIP-3009 authorizations locally; never submit a private key. A signed quote fixes the gas mode. Pending sponsor capacity is resumed on the same order. Fee-split payments still require buyer gas.

## Cash refunds (seller approval required)

- `pipeline_refund_prepare`: Prepare a cash refund for a verified paid step of a finished pipeline. This moves no money. The original seller must approve the exact EIP-3009 authorization locally; never send a private key. Refunds require seller cooperation and a configured gas sponsor.
- `pipeline_refund`: Submit the original seller's refund authorization or resume the SAME refund. The recipient is the original buyer, amount is the paid step price, and the sponsor pays gas. Preserve the exact authorization after a lost response. Returns a separately signed credit note; the original bill is unchanged.
- `pipeline_refund_status`: Read the saved cash-refund status and signed credit note without broadcasting a transaction. No private key or RPC is required. Pending means resume the same refund, never send a replacement transfer.
